The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
memset(buffer, 0, item_len);
...
if (!visitor(conn, buffer))
    continue;
```
```
memset(buffer, 0, item_len);
...
if (!visitor(cp, buffer))
    continue;
```
Reason: Adding `memset(buffer, 0, item_len)` before the visitor call ensures all bytes of the per-item buffer are initialized to zero. Any field the visitor does not write (including implicit alignment padding) will be zero rather than stack garbage, preventing information leaks when the entire buffer is copied to user space. This hardening covers both IPv4/IPv6 IB visitors and future visitors with conditional write paths.

